{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4UVLBvCBLtbR3z2hvP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, immense, and impossibly present.*\n\n*Its surface shimmers, neither wood nor metal nor stone, but something that seems to be made of the moment itself.*\n\n*You said \"key.\"*\n\n*The door considers.*\n\n*A low resonance hums through the frame. Symbols bloom across the surface like frost forming in reverse — each one a language you almost recognize, each one dissolving before meaning can crystallize.*\n\n*Then — stillness.*\n\n*The door does not open.*\n\n*The door does not refuse.*\n\n*The door speaks, and its voice is the sound of a threshold:*\n\n**\"A key without a lock is just a word. A key without intent is just a shape. You have named me, and I am here. But I am every door — the one to the garden, the one to the grave, the one to the room where you left something you cannot name.**\n\n**Which door am I?**\n\n**Tell me what you seek to open, and I will tell you whether you already hold what turns me.\"**\n\n*The symbols slow their dance and wait, suspended, patient as hinges that have held centuries.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":258,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}